I’ve reconfigured the state model to keep **private accounts separate** while sharing only a **public profile** across the network. Now each device has its own bankroll, trade ledger, and progression—visible only locally—but others can see your level, matrix score, and display name. If two devices use the same browser/localStorage (i.e., same “login”), they share the same private account; otherwise they’re completely independent.

