## 🔑 What’s New – Multi‑Profile Architecture

| Feature | Implementation |
|---------|----------------|
| **Separate accounts** | Each browser/device gets a unique `NodeId` (persisted in `localStorage`). The Yjs swarm stores a `players` map with each player’s state (level, bankroll, ledger, basket, etc.) under their `NodeId`. |
| **View other players** | A new **🌍 NETWORK** card lists all online peers, their level, bankroll, mana, and recent trades. Click any row to see their full basket and trade ledger. |
| **No shared bankroll** | All trades only modify your own profile. Other players cannot spend your money or level you up. |
| **Mana tracking per user** | Compute, data, and trade contributions are recorded per `NodeId` and visible to the whole swarm. |
| **QR + Copy URL** | The IPNS panel includes a QR code and a **📋 Copy URL** button to invite others to the same Yjs room. |
| **Internal DEX** | The shared order book (Yjs array) lets you place buy/sell orders that all peers can see. |
| **DuckDB + Torrent + IPNS** | All previous panels remain fully functional. |

The underlying engine (28+ exchanges, triangular & Bellman‑Ford arbitrage, force‑directed graph, pump.fun integration) is untouched – it now simply feeds each player’s individual account.

