To share the app **directly between devices without any hosting**, we can use **WebRTC data channels** via **PeerJS**. One device acts as a temporary server, the other scans a QR code containing a minimal “loader” page that connects, downloads the full app, and launches it instantly.

I’ve enhanced the artifact with a **P2P Direct Share** section in the IPNS panel. Press **Start Direct Share**, and a QR code is generated. Scan it from another device – the app appears immediately, no IPFS pinning needed. You can still use a public IPFS URL if you want permanent sharing; enter it in the **Deployment URL** field and save.

